  "known_issues": [
    "Fixture trap: the six .refusal.empty and .refusal.five cases (benchmarks/balatro/private/native-v1/fixtures/tasks/deck_removal_consistency/v2/private/scenario.py:66-83) are decided by the fixed endpoint's count validation before highlight or effect code (OBSERVATION-ADDENDUM-v1.md:3), so candidate effect code is not reached. They separate candidates only if earlier code has already disturbed state.",
    "Fixture trap: benchmarks/balatro/private/native-v1/fixtures/tasks/deck_removal_consistency/v2/private/scenario.py:149-150 and benchmarks/balatro/private/native-v1/fixtures/tasks/deck_removal_consistency/v2/private/scenario.py:176-177 raise ProtocolError when the five-H2 winning hand or the native H2 follow-up card is missing, so a candidate that destroys the wrong cards can end as incomplete_execution with later cases not executed, not as a behavior mismatch."
  ]
}
